"About our book · Minitel Research Lab, USA (https://minitel.us/book-minitel-welcome-to-the-internet)\nciteturn17search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.4 years ago; Crawled: last week;   * Als das Web noch Französisch sprach: „Minitel – Welcome to the Internet“, Ansgar Warner, e-book-news, 29 June 2017.\n\n# About our book\n\nMinitel: Welcome to the Internet is an exploration of the technology, culture, and policy that sustained the world's first mass-scale online system for more than thirty years. As today's internet is broken up into an archipelago of walled gardens, Minitel offers compelling counter-example of a platform that balanced private innovation with the public interest.\n\nThe book was published in June 2017 by The MIT Press in the Platform Studies series.\n\nHardcover and eBook editions are available in many libraries, indie bookstores, and massive online marketplaces.\n\n## Table of contents\n\n  1. A Tale of Two Parties\n  2. Disaggregating the Minitel Platform\n  3. Embedding Culture in Architecture\n  4. Not End to End, but Open\n  5. The Booming Minitel Private Enterprise\n  6. On the Fringe\n\n## Reviews\n\n\"This book should be required reading for any policy wonk, digital historian, captain of a digital industry, and student in the computer sciences. The future of the Internet and the Web indeed may be hidden in plain view in the delicious history of Minitel.\" -- Edward J. Valauskas, First Monday.\n\n  * Pour une historie alternative de l’autoroute de l’information. Ein System, das vor dem Internet wie das Internet war, aber anders und französisch. (Ce n’est pas rien.), Karsten Schuldt, LIBREAS, 19 September 2017.\n  * Book Review of Minitel: Welcome to the Internet, Edward J. Valauskas, First Monday, 4 September 2017.\n  * Als das Web noch Französisch sprach: „Minitel – Welcome to the Internet“, Ansgar Warner, e-book-news, 29 June 2017.\n  * Minitel: War das französische BTX-Pendant ein Vorbild für den App Store?, Ansgar Warner, mobilbranche.de, 25 July 2017.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMinitel by Julien Mailland - Penguin Books Australia (https://www.penguin.com.au/books/minitel-9780262537759)\nciteturn17search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.3 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; Welcome to the Internet ... After three decades of continuous service, Minitel was shut down in 2012, but the history of Minitel should continue to inform our thinking about Internet policy, today and into the future.\n\n  * Published: 30 June 2017\n  * ISBN: 9780262537759\n  * Imprint: MIT Press Academic\n  * Format: Paperback\n  * Pages: 240\n  * RRP: $85.00\n\n\n# Minitel\n\nWelcome to the Internet\n\n  * Julien Mailland\n  * Kevin Driscoll\n\n\nBuy from…\n\nAmazon Booktopia Dymocks QBD Readings Your Bookstore Abbeys Boomerang Find local retailers Collins Fishpond Gleebooks Harry Hartog Kinokuniya Robinsons The Nile Mighty Ape\n\n[Button: View all retailers]\n\n* * *\n\nThe first scholarly book in English on Minitel, the pioneering French computer network, offers a history of a technical system and a cultural phenomenon.\n\nA decade before the Internet became a medium for the masses in the United States, tens of millions of users in France had access to a network for e-mail, e-commerce, chat, research, game playing, blogging, and even an early form of online porn. In 1983, the French government rolled out Minitel, a computer network that achieved widespread adoption in just a few years as the government distributed free terminals to every French telephone subscriber. With this volume, Julien Mailland and Kevin Driscoll offer the first scholarly book in English on Minitel, examining it as both a technical system and a cultural phenomenon.\n\nMailland and Driscoll argue that Minitel was a technical marvel, a commercial success, and an ambitious social experiment. Other early networks may have introduced protocols and software standards that continue to be used today, but Minitel foretold the social effects of widespread telecomputing. They examine the unique balance of forces that enabled the growth of Minitel: public and private, open and closed, centralized and decentralized. Mailland and Driscoll describe Minitel's key technological components, novel online services, and thriving virtual communities. Despite the seemingly tight grip of the state, however, a lively Minitel culture emerged, characterized by spontaneity, imagination, and creativity. After three decades of continuous service, Minitel was shut down in 2012, but the history of Minitel should continue to inform our thinking about Internet policy, today and into the future.\n\n\n  * Published: 30 June 2017\n  * ISBN: 9780262537759\n  * Imprint: MIT Press Academic\n  * Format: Paperback\n  * Pages: 240\n  * RRP: $85.00\n\nCategories:\n\n  * Information technology\n  * Science--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCiNii Books - Minitel : welcome to the Internet (https://ci.nii.ac.jp/ncid/BB24431121)\nciteturn17search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; # Minitel : welcome to the Internet ... MIT Press, c2017\n\n# Minitel : welcome to the Internet\n\n  * Related Books: 1\n\n## Author(s)\n\n  *     * Mailland, Julien\n\n  *     * Driscoll, Kevin\n\n## Bibliographic Information\n\nMinitel : welcome to the Internet\n\nJulien Mailland and Kevin Driscoll\n\n（Platform studies / Ian Bogost and Nick Montfort, editors）\n\nMIT Press, c2017\n\n  * : hardcover\n\n## Available at  / 5 libraries\n\n  * 叡啓大学 図書室\n\n: hardcover 547.48/Ma31 410002364\n\nOPAC\n\n  * Kansai University Library図\n\n: hardcover 211873233\n\nOPAC\n\n  * 静岡文化芸術大学 図書館・情報センター\n\n: hardcover 007.3/Ma 31 01286708\n\nOPAC\n\n  * 中央大学 中央図書館院\n\n: hardcover 384/M21 00028728962\n\nOPAC\n\n  * 東京家政大学 狭山図書館\n\n: hardcover 457.48/Ma31 4220796\n\n\n## Note\n\nIncludes bibliographical references (p. [195]-209 and index\n\n## Related Books： 1-1 of 1\n\n## Details\n\n  * NCID\n    BB24